  "comment": "The constants C are nearly height-independent (algebraic in 1/x), because B is algebraic on every finite-support direction and M is fixed; the admissible error eta therefore decays with |h|, like x^A e^{-pi x/8}.  eta is a guarantee (no collision in V below that defect), saturated in direction only: the worst direction is the lowest free node, whose jet is algebraic in 1/x.  The prefactor depends on the class.  The unanchored row is the realistic one: the recurrence rows see delta_1 through d_1 = -2 delta_1 + delta_2 (a_0 = 1 fixed), and a change of 3e-5 in a_1 buys, under the normalization, the change of -0.12 in a_2 that the three-square control uses (its own recurrence defect, dominated by the third node, is about 1.4e5).  The strictly anchored class (delta_1 = 0 exactly) is an idealization in which the first free node is n = 3; even there eta crosses one near x = 82.  Measured relative to the carrier (divide B by |M_t|), the same numbers read as a conditioning constant growing like x^{-A} e^{pi x/8}."
